CM ============================================================
CM  TM-SC-NEC-009: Screwdriver Antenna — 80m Band
CM  2.4m whip, base loading coil, 4 horizontal elevated radials
CM  Frequency: 3.500–4.000 MHz (11 points, 0.050 MHz step)
CM
CM  Loading coil (series RL at base, segment 1 of GW1):
CM    R = 7.075 ohm  (Rcoil = Xant / Q, Q~240)
CM    X = 1698 ohm   (XL required to resonate 2.4m whip on 80m)
CM
CM  Whip: 2.4m, avg radius 0.006m, 20 segments
CM  Radials: 4 x 2.4m at z=0.005m, 90 deg spacing
CM  Ground: real (Sommerfeld-Norton), eps=13, sigma=0.005
CM  Feed: 1V voltage source at GW1, seg 1
CM
CM  Tuning note: 80m is the most challenging band for screwdriver
CM  operation. Quarter-wave at 3.75 MHz = 20.0m; whip is 12% of QW.
CM  Extreme loading required. Rcoil (7.075 ohm) >> Rrad (~0.5-1 ohm).
CM  System efficiency may be 5-15% (-8 to -13 dBd). Still useful
CM  for NVIS regional coverage. Coil Q is critical — use large-
CM  diameter, close-wound, silver-plated coil to maximize Q.
CM  Radial system and mount bond are as important as coil Q.
CM  FR sweep covers full 80/75m band: 3.500-4.000 MHz (US).
CM  Note: whip capacitance changes measurably with temperature
CM  at 80m; expect retuning needed during mobile operation.
CM ============================================================
CE
GW 1  20  0 0 0       0 0 2.4     0.006
GW 2   4  0 0 0.005   2.4 0 0.005  0.006
GW 3   4  0 0 0.005  -2.4 0 0.005  0.006
GW 4   4  0 0 0.005   0 2.4 0.005  0.006
GW 5   4  0 0 0.005   0 -2.4 0.005 0.006
GE 1
GN 2 0 0 0  13 0.005
LD 0  1  1  1  7.075  1698
EX 0  1  1  0  1  0
FR 0  11  0  0  3.500  0.050
RP 0  37  73  1000  0  0  5  5
EN
